    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Mormons believe that God the Father, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus Christ</a> and the Holy Ghost are three distinct beings, that Jesus's atonement saves all people, and that the faithful may attain godhood in the afterlife.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-smith">Joseph Smith</a> published the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-mormon">Book of Mormon</a> in 1830, which he said he had translated from golden plates, and organised the Church of Christ the same year; after he was killed in 1844 the largest group followed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigham-young">Brigham Young</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utah">Utah</a>.</li><li>The Utah-based <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-jesus-christ-of-latter-day-saints">LDS Church</a> banned plural marriage in 1890 and grew from about 1.7 million members in 1960 to a claimed 16 million in 2020, while over 400 denominations are estimated to have sprung from the movement.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>In the Mormon account of the pre-earthly life, all people first existed as spirits or &quot;intelligences&quot; in the presence of God, and a &quot;third&quot; of them, led by Satan, rejected his plan of salvation.</p></aside>
    </section>

